  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "What is the $\\text{GCF}$ of $9y$ and $6y?$",
  "worked_solution": "To find the GCF, we list the factors of the coefficients and identify any common variable factors in the expressions.\n\nThe factors of $9$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3,\\,9.\n$$\n\nThe factors of $6$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,2,\\,3,\\,6.\n$$\n\nThe common factors of $9$ and $6$ are\n\n$$\n1,\\,3.\n$$\n\nThe greatest of these common factors is $3.$\n\nNow we look at the variable factors. Both $9y$ and $6y$ contain $y.$\n\nThus, the greatest common factor of $9y$ and $6y$ is $3y.$",
